      "text": "To find the value of \\( a \\) for which \\( g(a) = 0 \\) for the function \\( g(x) = 3x - 4 \\), we need to substitute \\( a \\) into the function and set it equal to 0. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Start with the function:\n   \\[\n   g(x) = 3x - 4\n   \\]\n2. Set the function equal to 0:\n   \\[\n   3a - 4 = 0\n   \\]\n3. Solve for \\( a \\). First, add 4 to both sides of the equation:\n   \\[\n   3a - 4 + 4 = 0 + 4\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   3a = 4\n   \\]\n4. Divide both sides by 3:\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{4}{3}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( a \\) that satisfies \\( g(a) = 0 \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\\).",
