      "text": "To solve for \\( a \\) in the equation \\( g(a) = 0 \\) where \\( g(x) = 3x - 4 \\), we follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\( a \\) into the function \\( g(x) \\):\n   \\[\n   g(a) = 3a - 4\n   \\]\n\n2. Set \\( g(a) \\) equal to 0, as given in the problem:\n   \\[\n   3a - 4 = 0\n   \\]\n\n3. Solve the equation for \\( a \\):\n   \\[\n   3a - 4 = 0\n   \\]\n   Add 4 to both sides to isolate the term with \\( a \\):\n   \\[\n   3a = 4\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( a \\):\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{4}{3}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( a \\) for which \\( g(a) = 0 \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\\).\n\nA train 150 meters long takes 25.9979208136448 seconds to cross a bridge 175 meters long. What is the speed of the train in kmph?\n\nTo find the speed of the train, we need to determine the total distance the train travels and the total time it takes to travel that distance. The total distance is the sum of the length of the train and the length of the bridge, which is \\(150 + 175 = 325\\) meters. The total time taken is given as 25.9979208136448 seconds.\n\nFirst, we convert the time from seconds to hours to match the desired speed unit (kmph). There are 3600 seconds in an hour, so we convert 25.9979208136448 seconds to hours as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Time in hours} = \\frac{25.9979208136448}{3600} \\approx 0.0072216446704624  \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the speed of the train in meters per hour:\n\\[\n\\text{Speed in meters per hour} = \\frac{325 \\text{ meters}}{0.0072216446704624 \\text{ hours}} \\approx 44210.887 \\text{ m/h}\n\\]\n\nTo convert this speed to kilometers per hour, we use the conversion factor \\(1000 \\text{ meters} = 1 \\text{ kilometer}\\):\n\\[\n\\text{Speed in km/h} = \\frac{44210.887 \\text{ m/h}}{1000} = 44.210887 \\text{ km/h}\n\\]\n\nRounding to the nearest hundredth, the speed of the train is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{44.21}\n\\]\n\nEvaluate: $-\\left(\\sqrt{128}-\\sqrt{96}+\\sqrt{75}\\right)$.\n\nTo